Give DirectSound the same off switch ASIO already has.

The plugin drives the engine through SV_INIT_FLAG_USER_AUDIO_CALLBACK and
never opens a device, and the release audit holds a plugin's imports to the
core OS. Every backend the engine can compile out is therefore compiled out:
NOALSA and NOOSS on Linux and NOASIO on Windows already exist upstream and
are set from the build, but DirectSound has no switch even though every use
of it is already behind #ifdef DSOUND -- the WinCE build turns it off. Give
it the NODSOUND spelling the ASIO backend already uses, and dsound.dll,
dxguid.dll and ole32.dll go with it.

Waveform Audio has no such switch and stays: it is the unconditional
fallback driver, and winmm is linked regardless for the timer-resolution
calls in lib_sundog/main/main.cpp.

diff --git a/lib_sundog/sound/sound_win.hpp b/lib_sundog/sound/sound_win.hpp
index c4cb85c..174dbdc 100644
--- a/lib_sundog/sound/sound_win.hpp
+++ b/lib_sundog/sound/sound_win.hpp
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 // Windows: sound
 //
 
-#ifndef OS_WINCE
+#if !defined(OS_WINCE) && !defined(NODSOUND)
     #define DSOUND
 #endif
 #if !defined(OS_WINCE) && !defined(NOASIO)
